  "result": "The gate returned **OK** for LVMC_11_40_140_o1 on the first run after I wrote the rule and witnesses: 13 witnesses pass, 8 names are used, and the rule composes no other rule.\n\n**One mistake:** before writing anything, I ran the gate command once with a pipe added to it (`| head -0; true`). That broke the \"exact command only\" rule. It ran against the untouched skeletons and I discarded the output, so I don't know that verdict. It probably used one of the 6 runs.\n\n**The rule** (`library/TrafficSpec/Rules/LVMC_11/LVMC_11_40_140_o1.lean`):\n- **Who it covers:** any of the three admitted aggregates (bicycle, electric bicycle, electric scooter).\n- **When it applies:** for a sidewalk region the subject has just moved onto, in a declared business or residence district, when one of these holds:\n  - it is in an alley or driveway entrance at that moment or the observation before; or\n  - it was in no highway region the observation before; or\n  - it stays on that sidewalk until it leaves the highway (going into a building).\n- **What it requires:** a halt in the stopping zone (off the sidewalk, within the stop-point tolerance of it). The search runs back from the observation before the entry. It ends at the approach start or at the subject's previous entry onto that sidewalk, and is unknown if it reaches the start of the recording.\n- **Shared selection:** the obligation repeats the applicability's whole selection of the sidewalk.\n- **Narrowings:** none were needed.\n\n**The witnesses:** the six planned ones have their planned verdicts. I added `branch_2` to `branch_8` so every trigger alternative and class actually changes some witness's verdict: leaving and entering an alley, entering a driveway, leaving and entering a building, a second entry after an earlier halt, and a pedestrian.\n\n**One departure from the plan, in `blind`:** the planned story (\"no halt recorded\") can't come out unknown just because the region outlines are hidden. Either the subject's earlier time on the sidewalk ends the search and the result is violated, or the search runs back to the start of the recording. In that second case the result also carries a \"recording too short\" reason, which the gate rejects on this witness. So in my scene the bicycle stops once where it turns round inside the driveway, at a spot whose distance from the sidewalk the outline-less map can't give. The planner should change the `blind` narrative to allow that.\n\n`task_result.md` has the details, in `results/full221-1116-1018/iter-002/code/LVMC_11_40_140_o1/`.",
